  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Given intravenously, so bioavailability does not apply. Serum concentrations rise more than proportionally with dose, and its metabolic pathways are not known.",
    "substance": "The active moiety has a molecular weight of 924.09 and is intercalated into a liposomal membrane of true liposomes under 100 nm.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA and supplied as 50 mg vials for intravenous infusion.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning. Contraindicated with known hypersensitivity to the drug or any other constituent of the product.",
    "indication": "Empirical therapy for fungal infection in febrile neutropenic patients, cryptococcal meningitis in HIV patients, visceral leishmaniasis, and Aspergillus or Candida infections refractory to the conventional formulation.",
    "mechanism": "The label states no mechanism of action for this antifungal."
  },
  "tell": "A 100 to 153 hour terminal half-life, far beyond its 7 to 10 hour dosing-interval half-life, sets this liposomal polyene antifungal apart.",
